<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Ouargla</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1872 CE (approx.) · capital Ouargla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An oasis sultanate in the Algerian Sahara, ruling Ouargla's palm groves at a crossroads of caravan routes between the Maghreb and the Sahel.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ouargla had been an Ibadi and trading centre since the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, near the ruined city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sedrata">Sedrata</a>. A local sultanate is attested from around 1500, when chroniclers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-africanus">Leo Africanus</a> describe the town as a wealthy caravan stop with its own ruler.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans had limited power, mediating between the town's factions, the surrounding nomadic tribes such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaamba">Chaamba</a>, and Berber-speaking oasis farmers. The economy rested on date palms, irrigation and trade in slaves, gold and goods between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>. Ouargla paid tribute at times to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a> and competed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-touggourt">Sultanate of Touggourt</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The French extended their influence in the 1850s, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria</a> occupied Ouargla in 1872, ending the sultanate. The town later became the centre of the Algerian oil industry.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1500 CE – 1872 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.40%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1872 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ouargla</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber (Teggargrent), Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ouargla, Wargla</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=sultanate-of-ouargla" aria-label="Sultanate of Ouargla on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4817 1015 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Ouargla lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5137 1271L5077 1108M5137 1271L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5077 1108h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5137 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5137 1271h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ouargla. <a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=sultanate-of-ouargla">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

